      "title": "UV damage: remove and replace",
      "narration": "UV light can make adjacent cytosines and thymines bond covalently, distorting the DNA. Repair proteins recognize the damage, cut out the damaged section, replace the missing bases, and reseal the backbone.",
      "stage": {
        "bottom": 11
      },
